@*
    A collapsible group of input cards.

    The gear form has around forty inputs. Roughly fifteen decide the gear; the rest are
    ISO 6336 detail that most users leave alone. Showing them all at once made it impossible
    to tell which was which, so everything past the basics lives in one of these.

    Deliberately NOT <details>/<summary>: the browser reflects `open` back onto the element,
    so a user-toggled section and Blazor's render tree disagree about the attribute, and the
    next re-render — which this form does on nearly every keystroke, through @bind:after and
    the conditional fields — can slam it shut. Owning the flag here keeps it predictable.

    Collapsing hides inputs, so a collapsed section must still say what it is holding: pass
    State a short live summary of the current values. A section the user never opens should
    still be honest about what it is doing to their calculation.

    Styles live in wwwroot/css/modern-icons.css, not in a <style> block here — a Razor
    <style> only reaches the DOM once that page has rendered, so a user deep-linking straight
    into a calculator would get an unstyled form.
*@

<div class="advanced-section @(isOpen ? "is-open" : null)">
    <button type="button" class="advanced-head" aria-expanded="@isOpen" @onclick="Toggle">
        <span class="advanced-chevron" aria-hidden="true">&#9656;</span>
        <span class="advanced-heading">
            <span class="advanced-title">@Title</span>
            @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(Summary))
            {
                <span class="advanced-summary">@Summary</span>
            }
        </span>
        @if (State is not null)
        {
            <span class="advanced-state">@State</span>
        }
    </button>

    @if (isOpen)
    {
        <div class="advanced-body">
            @ChildContent
        </div>
    }
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string Title { get; set; } = "";

    /// <summary>One line on what lives in here, shown while collapsed.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Summary { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// A live digest of the current settings, e.g. "ISO 53 profile B, k calculated".
    /// This is what stops a collapsed section from hiding a decision.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? State { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Start expanded. Use for a section the user has just been sent to.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool InitiallyOpen { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }

    private bool isOpen;

    protected override void OnInitialized() => isOpen = InitiallyOpen;

    private void Toggle() => isOpen = !isOpen;
}
